HST Office: a document closed while the feature search is open no longer deletes the search twice.

CommandPopupHandler (owned by SfxViewFrame) keeps the open feature search (CommandListBox) and
deletes it from the popover's closed handler (PopupModeEnd -> mpListBox.reset()). A popover that is
destroyed while still shown pops itself down (~SalInstancePopover -> ImplPopDown -> signal_closed).
When the view frame closes with the search open, ~SfxViewFrame -> m_pCommandPopupHandler.reset()
-> ~CommandListBox -> ~SalInstancePopover -> PopupModeEnd -> mpListBox.reset() deletes the list box
that is being destroyed (a std::unique_ptr does not clear itself in its destructor): its members are
destroyed and freed a second time.

Windows r1-auto W9 (Alt+Q, then the document closed over UNO) died with heap corruption
0xC0000374 in that free (ProcDump full dump, run 42779319665: SwXTextDocument::close ->
~SfxViewFrame -> ~SalInstancePopover -> PopupModeEnd -> ~CommandListBox -> free; after the heap
error the second ~CommandListBox called release() through a cleared interface).

~CommandListBox now disconnects the closed handler first: whoever destroys the list box already
owns that deletion, so nothing is lost. Inherited from upstream (same code in 26.8).

License: modified upstream files keep their license (MPL-2.0).

--- a/sfx2/inc/commandpopup/CommandPopup.hxx
+++ b/sfx2/inc/commandpopup/CommandPopup.hxx
@@ -124,16 +124,17 @@
     void addFindInDocumentRow(OUString const& rText);
 
 public:
     /** HST Office: pAnchor (in pParent coordinates) is the feature search box of the ribbon tab
         row, the popup opens under it; rInitialText is typed and searched at once. */
     CommandListBox(weld::Window* pParent, css::uno::Reference<css::frame::XFrame> const& xFrame,
                    tools::Rectangle const* pAnchor = nullptr,
                    OUString const& rInitialText = OUString());
+    ~CommandListBox();
     void connect_closed(const Link<weld::Popover&, void>& rLink)
     {
         mxPopover->connect_closed(rLink);
     }
 };
 
 class CommandPopupHandler final
 {
--- a/sfx2/source/commandpopup/CommandPopup.cxx
+++ b/sfx2/source/commandpopup/CommandPopup.cxx
@@ -449,16 +449,25 @@
         // the character typed into the search box: searched at once, the cursor after it
         mpEntry->set_text(rInitialText);
         mpEntry->set_position(-1);
         ModifyHdl(*mpEntry);
     }
     mpEntry->grab_focus();
 }
 
+CommandListBox::~CommandListBox()
+{
+    // The popover pops down when it is destroyed while still shown (its view frame closes with the
+    // search open) and then calls its closed handler. That handler is the owner's PopupModeEnd, which
+    // deletes this list box: a second delete of the box that is being destroyed. Nobody is told any
+    // more that a popover closes which is being destroyed.
+    mxPopover->connect_closed(Link<weld::Popover&, void>());
+}
+
 IMPL_LINK_NOARG(CommandListBox, QueryTooltip, const weld::TreeIter&, OUString)
 {
     size_t nSelected = mpCommandTreeView->get_selected_index();
     if (nSelected < maCommandList.size())
     {
         auto const& rCurrent = maCommandList[nSelected];
         return rCurrent.m_aTooltip;
     }
